{"path":"utility/bitset/operator_at","title":"std::bitset<N>::operator[]","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::bitset&lt;N&gt;::</span>operator[]","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/bitset/operator_at","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Accesses the bit at position pos. The first version returns the value of the bit, the second version returns an object of type std::bitset::reference that allows modification of the value.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> operator<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> pos <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(constexpr since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">reference operator<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> pos <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(constexpr since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Accesses the bit at position <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pos</span></code>. The first version returns the value of the bit, the second version returns an object of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset/reference\">std::bitset::reference</a></span> that allows modification of the value.\n</p><p>Unlike <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset/test\">test()</a></span>, does not throw exceptions: the behavior is undefined if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pos</span></code> is out of bounds.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> pos\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> position of the bit to return\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> The value of the requested bit.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> An object of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset/reference\">std::bitset::reference</a></span>, which allows writing to the requested bit.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;bitset&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstddef&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset\"><span class=\"kw1034\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bitset</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nu0\">8</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> b1<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu6\">0b00101010</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// binary literal for 42</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> i <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> b1.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"b1[\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"]: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> b1<span class=\"br0\">[</span>i<span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    b1<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// modifies the first bit through bitset::reference</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"After setting bit 0, b1 holds \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> b1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>b1[0]: 0\nb1[1]: 1\nb1[2]: 0\nb1[3]: 1\nb1[4]: 0\nb1[5]: 1\nb1[6]: 0\nb1[7]: 0\nAfter setting bit 0, b1 holds 00101011</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue11\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 11</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>1. the description was missing in the C++ standard<br>2. there was only the non-const overload\n</td>\n<td>1. description added<br>2. added the const overload\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue907\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 907</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>the behavior of reading the bit at <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">pos</span></code> was equivalent<br>to that of <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset/test\"><code>test(pos)</code></a>, but <code>test()</code> may throw exceptions\n</td>\n<td>avoids mentioning <code>test()</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset/test\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>test</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  accesses specific bit <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/bitset","title":"std::bitset"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::bitset<N>::operator[]","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Accesses the bit at position pos."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"pos"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The value of the requested bit."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"test","note":"accesses specific bit"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++23"],"wordCount":265,"codeBlockCount":2}
